 "insight": [
  "The trend of import concentration by product chapters in Luxembourg from 2005 to 2025 shows mixed changes across key products.",
  "Imports of plastics and articles thereof increased significantly by 118.2%, from 592.6 million euros in 2005 to 1.29 billion euros in 2025, peaking at 1.64 billion euros in 2022.",
  "In contrast, imports of iron and steel decreased by 24.1%, from 1.26 billion euros in 2005 to 953.8 million euros in 2025, with a peak of 2.02 billion euros in 2008.",
  "Imports of mineral fuels and oils rose by 27.8%, from 1.75 billion euros in 2005 to 2.23 billion euros in 2025, peaking at 4.00 billion euros in 2022.",
  "These values are nominal and not adjusted for price changes, and 4.8% of the import value is confidential at full product detail."
 ],
